     "content_html": "The actin head forms a cross-bridge with myosin, which initiates the power stroke. During the power stroke, the actin head bends with the release of ADP and inorganic phosphate. Another ATP binds to the actin head, causing the cross-bridge to detach and returning actin to the cocked configuration."
    }
